<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duong Tam Kha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dương Tam Kha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duong Tam Kha was a Vietnamese ruler who seized the throne of the Ngo dynasty after the death of his brother-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-quyen">Ngo Quyen</a> in 944, ruling as Duong Binh Vuong. Ngo Quyen's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-xuong-van">Ngo Xuong Van</a> overthrew him in 950 but spared his life. The usurpation weakened the dynasty and opened the way to the period of the Twelve Warlords.</p></div>
